Reject loose bound variables instead of panicking

eval, eval_spine, infer_value and infer_nonvar looked up a de Bruijn
variable in the closure environment / local context with
.expect("... loose bvar ..."), so an export whose declaration (or a
definition unfolded while checking an inductive, which sokonanoda checks
while parsing, before the definitions) contains a variable not bound by
an enclosing binder crashed the checker with an internal error. Lean's
kernel rejects such terms ("type checker does not support loose bound
variables"); these sites now reject too. Found by the arena's
bugs/loose-bvar-value test and nano-lean's invalid-loose-bvar fixtures;
repro inputs in suite-repros. Regression tests in infer.rs.
Upstream: open issue intgrah/sokonanoda#6 (by jasisz, 2026-10-27) reports this
exit-3 internal error on the arena's loose-bvar-value test; no fix yet.

